From 59425f3cd0f8d7df3dd9faff268a1f039649c581 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Data-crea <sattler.daniel@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:25:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] OrionLayer Open Fix 34: send the save slots for the main
 menu's Load dialog too (ext_api.cpp)

What changed: SerializeSaveSlots also sends MSG_SAVE_SLOTS when the
current screen is SCREEN_MAIN_MENU and MOX::_screen_data is 2, not only
on SCREEN_GAME. One condition, marked with an OrionLayer comment.

Why: the main menu's LOAD GAME runs the GAME popup's Load builder
(MAINMENU::Mainmenu_Load_Game_Popup_, mainmenu.cpp:187-189, which sets
_screen_data 2 while the screen stays SCREEN_MAIN_MENU), so a client saw
the dialog's ten rows but nothing in them and could not draw it. With
the slots on the wire OrionLayer draws it in HD as it draws the in-game
Load dialog (open fix 14). Recorded in orionlayerv3
doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md, entry 34.

Ported onto orion2re v2.0.0 in scratch (work order 242 e) from local 9ab84230:
renamed 3-way merge (identifier map cf4d9617->v2.0.0), clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/ext/ext_api.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
index b455fa6f..147a2861 100644
--- a/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
+++ b/src/ext/ext_api.cpp
@@ -478,7 +478,11 @@ static void SerializeFields(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf) {
 static bool SerializeSaveSlots(std::vector<uint8_t>& buf,
                                int16_t current_screen) {
     buf.clear();
-    if (current_screen != SCREEN_GAME) {
+    // OrionLayer change, Open Fix 34 (orionlayerv3 doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md):
+    // the main menu's Load dialog (screen_data 2) sends its save slots too.
+    const bool main_menu_load = current_screen == SCREEN_MAIN_MENU
+                                && MOX::screen_data == 2;
+    if (current_screen != SCREEN_GAME && !main_menu_load) {
         return false;
     }
     const int16_t screen_data = MOX::screen_data;
